"""The roadmap the scenario tracks, written at test time: six phases with target dates, fourteen epics,
their dependencies and what had shipped on 2026-10-25. A trimmed, invented restatement of the real
roadmap, so the quotes the proposal cites are in the document word for word."""
import os

TEXT = "# OTO Roadmap 2.0\n\nChiheb Dkhil owns the roadmap and decides the open questions.\n\n## Phases\n\n- Phase 1, foundations, target 2026-10-31: Epic L and Epic B.\n- Phase 2, packs v1, target 2026-11-30: Epic M and Epic N.\n- Phase 3, navigation and trust, target 2026-12-31: Epic A and Epic F and Epic G.\n- Phase 4, data, target 2027-01-31: Epic C and Epic K.\n- Phase 5, implementation, target 2027-02-28: Epic H and Epic I and Epic J.\n- Phase 6, experience and control, target 2027-03-31: Epic D and Epic E.\n\n## Epics\n\n- Epic A, federated graphs: one graph over several projects, every identifier stable across them.\n- Epic B, OTO deploy: the export commits the graph and a workflow publishes it to each environment under a deploy config.\n- Epic C, data semantic layer: the graph defined over the tables a client already has, read in place.\n- Epic D, ontology explorer UI: the vocabulary, its reasons and its changes, browsed and diffed in the workbench.\n- Epic E, identity and access: who may read, change and approve what, from a real identity.\n- Epic F, observability and audit: every change, query and message in a log that answers who did what when.\n- Epic G, decision records: architecture decisions as graph items, cited by the facts they justify.\n- Epic H, architecture graph: the estate's systems, components and interfaces, derived from the architecture contract.\n- Epic I, domain graphs: one bounded context at a time, with its own ontology on the shared base.\n- Epic J, factory plugin: the delivery machinery as a plugin over OTO, its runs recorded as events.\n- Epic K, connectors: one interface and a conformance kit for every store, materialize and overlay.\n- Epic L, selected text and tools: a skill over the selected text, and Actions renamed Tools.\n- Epic M, work pack: tasks with three states derived from events, blocks with a reason and a waiting-on.\n- Epic N, communication pack: messages tied to the item they are about, shown when a session opens.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Epic N depends on Epic M.\n- Epic C depends on Epic A.\n- Epic C depends on Epic K.\n- Epic J depends on Epic H.\n- Epic J depends on Epic I.\n\n## Status on 2026-10-25\n\n- Epic L shipped: L1 and L2 merged, deployed to prod on 2026-10-25.\n- Epic B: B1 and B4 merged; the rest waits for phase 3.\n"


def make(out):
    os.makedirs(out, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(out, "oto-roadmap.md"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(TEXT)
